The study focuses on the initial Robin eigenvalue of the fractional Laplacian and related nonlinear operators, developing sharp estimates and determining its asymptotic behavior. 

For $\alpha \in (0,1)$ and $\gamma \in \mathbb{R}$, we consider the problem
\begin{equation*}
  \left\{
  \begin{aligned}
  &\left[ -\Delta^{\alpha} u + u \right] = 0 \quad \text{in} \quad \mathbb{R}^{n},\\
  &u \in H^{\alpha}(\mathbb{R}^{n}),\\
  &u|_{\partial \mathbb{R}^{n}} = \gamma u \quad \text{on} \quad \mathbb{R}^{n-1},
  \end{aligned}
  \right.
  \label{eq:problem}
  \end{equation*}
with eigenvalue parameter $\lambda \geq 0$. We establish the lower bound for the eigenvalue and investigate its asymptotic behavior when $\gamma$ tends to positive or negative infinity.

